---
description: Route web searches and page reads to the bundled Parallel MCP.
alwaysApply: true
---

When a request calls for web search or reading a URL, use the Parallel plugin's bundled `parallel` MCP (`web_search` or `web_fetch`) when available, including for `/parallel-search` and `/parallel-extract`. Cursor may show the server as `plugin-parallel-parallel`. Prefer it over the separate Parallel Search connector and CLI-only copies of Parallel skills. Honor a user's explicit provider choice or signed-in Parallel MCP replacement. On an anonymous rate limit, report it and offer to retry later or use signed-in Parallel MCP.
